Test hooks for flycast used by tools/audio_regress.sh, tools/audiocheck.py and tools/vmulcd.py (not part of the port).
Applies to flycast 7adbf3caef251b153e348df3f469a0f35878339d (github.com/flyinghead/flycast) with
`git apply`; each hook does nothing unless its environment variable is set.

  FC_AUDIO_DUMP=<file>  write the AICA's 44.1 kHz output as raw s16 stereo (L, R)
  FC_RAMDUMP=<file>     when the guest prints a serial line "FCDUMP <addr> <len>" (hex), write that
                        range of main RAM to <file> (AUDIODUMP builds hand over their records so)
  FC_VMULCD=<file>      one line per VMU LCD write: sequence number, VMU port (A1...), the 192 raw
                        bytes in hex (tools/vmulcd.py reads it)

